Design a circuit that checks the validity of a 3-bit input tuple based on specific XOR relationships. The output `valid` is asserted true if the XOR of the first two bits matches the third bit, the XOR of the last two bits matches the first bit, and the XOR of the first and third bits matches the second bit. This module effectively functions as a validity checker for tuples under defined conditions.
