description:
Design a Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) generator that outputs a pulse signal with a variable duty cycle based on a control input. The PWM signal is governed by a clock input, allowing precise modulation of the signal's width. The duty cycle is defined as a function of the control signal, converting it into an appropriate number of bits for representation. When the duty cycle is greater than zero, the output pulse is driven high; otherwise, it is driven low, and the duty cycle is decremented on each clock edge, enabling a scaled modulation effect.
module top_module(
  input ctrl, // control signal
  input clk, // clock signal
  output reg pwm // pulse signal with variable duty cycle
);

code:
module top_module(
  input ctrl, // control signal
  input clk, // clock signal
  output reg pwm // pulse signal with variable duty cycle
);parameter n = 8; // number of bits used to represent the duty cycle

// other internal signals and variables
reg [n-1:0] duty_cycle;

// define the duty cycle as a function of the control signal
always @ (ctrl)
begin
  duty_cycle = ctrl * (2**n-1);
end

// use the duty cycle to adjust the pulse signal generated by the clock signal
always @ (posedge clk)
begin
  if (duty_cycle > 0)
    pwm <= 1;
  else
    pwm <= 0;
  duty_cycle <= duty_cycle - 1;
end

endmodule

