description:
Design a one-bit shift register with an 8-bit storage capacity. On each rising edge of the clock signal (C), the shift register shifts in a new bit (I) from the least significant end, while the most significant bit (bit 7) is routed to the output (O). This module effectively captures a sequence of bits over time, with the latest input being shifted into the register, allowing for serial input data processing.
module top_module(
    input  wire I,
    input  wire C,
    output wire O
);

code:
module top_module(
    input  wire I,
    input  wire C,
    output wire O
);reg [7:0] shift_register;

  always @(posedge C) shift_register <= {shift_register[6:0], I};

  assign O = shift_register[7];

endmodule

