description:
Design a circuit that toggles a 16-bit LED output every four clock cycles, effectively creating a flashing LED effect. The circuit resets the LED output and the internal delay counter to zero upon receiving a reset signal. When operating, the circuit increments a delay counter with each clock pulse; once the counter reaches a threshold of three, it resets and inverts the LED output, achieving a blinker effect.
