description:
Design a 4-input priority multiplexer where the highest-priority input with a binary value of '1' will determine the output. The module takes a 4-bit input and generates a single output based on the highest active bit position: if only one input line is active, the corresponding output is selected; if multiple inputs are active, the lowest position takes priority. If no inputs are active, the output defaults to zero. This functionality is particularly useful in applications where priority signaling is essential.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg out
);reg [1:0] select;

always @* begin
    case(in)
        4'b0001: select = 2'b00;
        4'b0010: select = 2'b01;
        4'b0100: select = 2'b10;
        4'b1000: select = 2'b11;
        default: select = 2'b00;
    endcase
end

always @* begin
    case(select)
        2'b00: out = in[0];
        2'b01: out = in[1];
        2'b10: out = in[2];
        2'b11: out = in[3];
        default: out = 1'b0;
    endcase
end

endmodule

