Implement a UART (Universal Asynchronous Receiver-Transmitter) transmitter module that serially transmits an 8-bit data input. The module takes in a clock signal, reset signal, and a data valid signal, and outputs the serialized data bit via SOut. It supports optional features such as parity checking and stop bits based on given parameters. The transmission process is controlled by counting clock cycles to achieve the specified baud rate, and it only activates when the data is valid and ready to transmit. The output SOut sends the data in the format of start bit, data bits, optional parity bit, and stop bits, allowing for reliable serial communication.
