description:
Develop a binary to BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) converter for an 8-bit binary input. The module takes an 8-bit binary number as input and produces a 10-bit BCD output. It uses a shift-and-add-3 algorithm to convert the binary value to BCD format, which is suitable for driving seven-segment displays or other BCD-based systems. The process involves shifting the binary number left while adjusting nibbles that exceed the BCD limit (greater than 4) by adding 3, ultimately providing the converted BCD value as output.
module top_module(
  input wire [7:0] b,
  output reg [9:0] p
);

code:
module top_module(
  input wire [7:0] b,
  output reg [9:0] p
);reg [17:0] z;
  integer i;
  always @ (*)
  begin
    for(i=0;i<=17;i=i+1)
	  z[i] = 0;
	  z[10:3] = b;
	  repeat(5)
	  begin
	    if(z[11:8]>4)
		  z[11:8] = z[11:8] + 3;
		if(z[15:12]>4)
		  z[15:12] = z[15:12] + 3;
		  z[17:1] = z[16:0];
	  end
      p = z[17:8];
  end
endmodule

