description:
Design a circuit that swaps adjacent pairs of bits in an 8-bit input vector. For each pair of bits (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), and (6,7), the output vector will have the second bit of each pair copied to the first position and the first bit copied to the second position, effectively rearranging the bits.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] input_vector,
  output reg [7:0] output_vector
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] input_vector,
  output reg [7:0] output_vector
);integer i;

  always @ (input_vector) begin
    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 2) begin
      output_vector[i] = input_vector[i+1];
      output_vector[i+1] = input_vector[i];
    end
  end

endmodule

